# RIDENOVA MASTER FIX PROMPT — RIDE REQUEST LIFECYCLE, REAL-TIME ACCEPTANCE, 5-MINUTE TIMER, FARE INCREASE, AND PERSISTENT ADMIN-APPROVED DRIVER VERIFICATION

## PRIMARY OBJECTIVE

Fix the existing RideNova application by implementing the missing ride-request features and correcting the driver-verification workflow. The current application displays “Ride Requested Successfully” and “Searching for a driver... (requested),” but the customer cannot see a countdown timer, cannot increase the offered fare, and does not receive real-time notifications when a driver accepts a ride. The customer must refresh the page to see the updated status. In addition, drivers are automatically approved after submitting their documents, without an actual admin approval process, and previously saved driver approval statuses do not reliably persist across code updates, refreshes, or redeployments.

These are functional defects, not merely design issues. Implement actual working changes across the existing React frontend, Express backend, PostgreSQL/Supabase database, Clerk authentication, and Supabase Realtime integration.

**Do not return only an audit, explanation, plan, or list of suggested changes. Modify the actual existing project files, implement the features, run the relevant tests, and verify the results.**

