- Reject the API request.
- Keep the persisted online status false.
- Display a professional explanation.
- Provide a link to the driver's verification status.

Example:

“Admin approval required”

“Your driver application is still under review. You can go online once an administrator approves your application.”

The online/offline UI must reflect the backend response, not just update a local React state variable.

Prevent unauthorized direct API requests from changing driver availability.

When an approved driver becomes unavailable for a valid reason, update the persisted status and remove the driver from eligible dispatch results.

Do not interfere with an active-trip restriction already implemented in the project. An active on-demand trip must not be abandoned by switching offline. Future scheduled rides should follow the existing scheduling rules and should not unnecessarily force the driver to stay online continuously.

